/*
  0.1.0 golden coverage (P2 — the feature the Plan A final review requested):
  a revisit <hub> (§7.3.2), `<when is="…">` literal-pattern arms (§7.3.1), and
  {{…}} content interpolation (§7.6), all against `--project docs/examples/showcase`.

  Plan C: `<hub>` LOWERING is DONE. A hub PASSES `lute check` AND COMPILES to a
  `hub` record (IR A2) via `lute compile`, so this file is exercised by BOTH the
  check and compile `--project` integration tests (`hub_demo_example_checks_clean`
  + `hub_demo_example_compiles`).
*/

# S01EP02 — The Revisit

## Closing Up

/*
  Content-line interpolation (§7.6): `{{userName}}` is the always-renderable
  reserved token; `{{run.affection}}` is a DECLARED path (number, default 0 ->
  definitely assigned -> renders clean, no E-UNDECLARED / E-MAYBE-UNSET).
*/
@narrator: Venny's again, and Marina is closing up. Good to see you, {{userName}}.
@marina{code="0010" emotion="delighted" variant="1"}: You came back! Warmth so far: {{run.affection}}.

## The Revisit Menu

/*
  <hub> (§7.3.2, §11.1.3): a revisit menu. The no-dead-end obligation
  (E-HUB-NO-EXIT) is satisfied by `leave` — an UNGUARDED `exit` choice.
  `askCoffee` is `once` (drops from the eligible set after one pick);
  `compliment` is a `when`-guarded sticky choice whose guard is a schema @ref
  (`helped`, cel `run.metHelpfully`, a default-bool -> definitely assigned).
  The hub implicitly folds `scene.choices.chatWithMarina` (enum of choice ids
  U `unset`) and `scene.visited.chatWithMarina.<choiceId>: bool` (default false).
*/
<hub id="chatWithMarina">
  <choice id="askCoffee" label="Ask about the coffee" once>
    @marina{code="0020" emotion="content" variant="0"}: House blend. Bold, like the clientele.
  </choice>
  <choice id="compliment" label="Say she was kind earlier" when="@helped">
    @fixer{code="0030"}: You were gentle about it before. It stuck with me.
    ::set{scene.affect.marina += 1}
  </choice>
  <choice id="leave" label="Head out" exit>
    @fixer{code="0040"}: I'd better get moving.
  </choice>
</hub>

## Reading the Visit

/*
  `<when is="…">` literal-pattern arms (§7.3.1) over the hub's implicit
  recording enum `scene.choices.chatWithMarina` (choice ids U `unset`). FULL
  `is` coverage is exhaustive WITHOUT an <otherwise> (§11.2, the normative path).
*/
<match on="scene.choices.chatWithMarina">
  <when is="askCoffee">
    @fixer{mono}: Coffee talk. Safe ground.
  </when>
  <when is="compliment">
    @fixer{mono}: I said the kind thing, and meant it.
  </when>
  <when is="leave">
    @fixer{mono}: Straight for the door.
  </when>
  <when is="unset">
    @fixer{mono}: I never engaged at all.
  </when>
</match>

/*
  A `bool` `<when is>` pair over the per-choice visited flag
  `scene.visited.chatWithMarina.askCoffee` (default false) — the second
  recording namespace the hub folds. `is="true"|"false"` covers the bool domain.
*/
<match on="scene.visited.chatWithMarina.askCoffee">
  <when is="true">
    @marina{code="0050" emotion="content" variant="0"}: You already know the blend.
  </when>
  <when is="false">
    @marina{code="0060" emotion="neutral" variant="0"}: Curious about the menu?
  </when>
</match>
